usage: python3 -m quality [-h] [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--report-dir REPORT_DIR]
                          {truth} [ids ...]

Independent d/p/q oracle, derived from README/spec densities. Points: sampler
and fitted parameters, then one-coordinate stresses, ordered by README
parameter order. Positive distances to a single bound are multiplied by .1 and
10; finite intervals move 90% towards each edge; unbounded nonzero coordinates
are multiplied by .1 and 10 (zero moves to -1 and +1). Integer, design, fixed
and endpoint coordinates remain at the fitted golden value. Family-local
special_points take priority over stresses. At most eight historical points,
plus the README default if absent. Sampling selects the default and fit. No
shared distribution registry: optional truth.py beside README supplies a high-
precision antiderivative/support correction or a documented gap. Routes are
verified against the declarative density, not against C++, scipy or R.

positional arguments:
  {truth}
  ids

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --timeout TIMEOUT     wall-clock seconds per family (default: 900)
  --report-dir REPORT_DIR
                        directory for per-family generation status
